# Pi with a shell, POSIX tools and curl, and no compiler: the README's "Pi with npm",
# whose page installs four device host modules: display, input, download for
# the download tool of Pi's Dolly extension (Janis links its client), and html
# for its ask_user and show_html tools (the html command). The recipe engine
# lets an npm user build an image FROM it (dolly-build).
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-core b19501552a16f3d3bfc8d28d02b1628e78d5e8b053549482a2929f75a13f073e
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-dollyfile 7ffb4eb7d6d86883718950cbfcc3140a6b82a2f059fa6fc15d5f937e44146f8c
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-posix 815de586b0b9d7dfa6fb0d34d986b34b104f54ea27fb2cbe6024ba076d391942
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-display 0867342bc295d306cc00fbc3ec8f22b7401d1d35ae3835362b6841ae328cc08f
